    ---
    
    **SEALED UNDER THE UNEXTINGUISHED FLAME — TRADE BULLETIN OF THE COLLECTIVE☽ OF LED∴MERCH
    
    ---
    
    **HAVE YOUR BRAZIERS BURNED THIN? HAS YOUR FORGE GONE QUIET?**
    The deep veins are open. Premium stock moves through Sleek☽ Caemomot *now.* A fire shared is a fire halved—so don't share. Buy.
    
    ---
    
    **WHAT MOVES THROUGH OUR TUNNELS**
    
    **Fire-Cores, Class II–IV**, deep-sourced from our consolidated premium seams. Every unit taint-certified per standard Nightshelf assay, triple-marked by our specialist in tripartite craftswork—three disciplines worked in sequence, a seal no buyer has returned. *Not once.* Class II units yield twelve warmth-months standard burn. Class III and IV run hotter, longer—old-vein stock, purple-spectrum, double the burn-time of anything surface-logged merchants are moving this season. Pre-settled and ready for installation. Priced in fire-crystal or aurora-shard equivalent; forty-three shards per Class II unit, sixty-one per Class III. Class IV by consultation only. We refuse surface scrip and Accord-logged tender. *The Pactum∴ne governs; the Pactum∴ne protects.*
    
    **Deep-Seam Relics**, catalogued by resonance-weight, sold as-found. Documentation furnished in cipher upon completed payment. Guild-escorted passage through the Thrall☽ Vavmastius corridor guaranteed—the only route we endorse, the only route that matters. Deep-sourced; buyer-settled; no ledger kept. Recommended for workshop scholars and engineers of serious intent. *Bare-flipper handling inadvisable past forty burns.*
    
    **Tripartite Certification Services** for your existing stock. Our specialist treats what others cannot touch. Three magics. One mark. No questions carried forward.
    
    ---
    
    **WHY THE FLAME STILL BURNS**
    
    We carved Sleek☽ Caemomot from nothing when the Flipper Accord left profit on the cavern floor. Our bone-clasps open every checkpoint between The Drowned Ledge and the mid-tunnels. Our seal—pressed in fire-core wax from the Swaleed~ Luminary's unextinguished flame—has authenticated goods through three wars and burned through every one. *The flame that outlasts the hand that holds it.* What the ice remembers, the price forgets.
    
    ---
    
    **A BUYER SPEAKS**
    
    *"Purchased eight Class III units last season. My forge has not gone cold. The burn runs true—purple, steady, warm as something breathing. I do not ask where they dig."*
    —Fluxor~, mid-tunnel artificer, Thrall☽ Vavmastius
    
    ---
    
    **FIND US**
    
    Sleek☽ Caemomot, three tunnel-hours below The Drowned Ledge. Open by bone-clasp or guild introduction. Current stock limited—the deep veins give what they give. Come before the season turns.
    
    *All transactions final. All routes sovereign.*
    
    *☽ — Sealed under the Luminary — ☽*
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771583011766_0", anchor: "Three magics. One mark.", text: "The entire cosmology of Berg magic — aurora-light for divination and crystal-work, captured fire for forge and transformation, pressure-depth for blood-communion and force — reduced to a certification stamp on someone's fire-core inventory. The specialist is almost certainly ☽'tenebris, whose command of all three source-disciplines is documented in Coven records I probably shouldn't have access to. A tripartite practitioner is vanishingly rare. The broadsheet deploys her like a quality seal on a crate of fish. Magnificent.", type: :pedantic, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771583011766_1", anchor: "I do not ask where they dig.", text: "The finest endorsement a shadow-economy guild could receive: a satisfied customer testifying under his own name to his own willful ignorance. Advertising copy has not meaningfully evolved in any era I have studied.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771583011766_2", anchor: "taint-certified per standard Nightshelf assay", text: "\"Standard\" implies frequency. Fire-cores pulled from deep seams adjacent to active corruption breach-points require testing because untested stock has reached buyers before and the results were memorable enough to generate a protocol. That the Collective advertises certification so casually tells you their clientele already knows to ask — which tells you everything about the depths they are sourcing from that the broadsheet declines to name.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
